#X text 20 20 m_404 -- the Roland SP-404MKII's device layer \, and the only file that talks to it. Both directions: pads in on param \, pads out from u_map's cord \, over sixteen notes on ten channels. ref/device/sp404.md, f 84;
#X text 20 130 creation arg 1: the Pd channel the 404's own channel 1 \, bank A \, lands on (33 on the device) \, required. No port argument: noteout's channel encodes the port. inlet 1: selector-prefixed -- pad <1..160> <velocity>. outlets: none \, everything goes on param and err., f 84;
#X text 900 20 160 pads \, one formula: the bank is the channel (A to J are Pd channels 33 to 42) and the pad is the note \, the same sixteen in every bank (items 195 and 196)., f 84;
#X text 1900 20 Not 47 + n: the rows run downward in blocks of four. m_404.lua holds the map (item 190 \, ref/device/sp404.md)., f 84;
#X text 20 3400 One table \, both directions: receive looks up the pad for a note \, transmit the note for a pad \, both in m_404.lua \, so there is no second copy to drift., f 66;
#X text 1220 3400 In the Lua rather than a file: the pad map is a device fact checked once \, where cut-it-map.txt is configuration that changes. docs-check compares it with the table on ref/device/sp404.md., f 66;
#X text 2420 3400 m_nano's channel gate \, ten wide \, and the offset is the bank. The Launchpad sits 32 below and the Volca 16 above., f 66;
#X text 20 3640 The bank is the channel's offset from bank A \, and the Lua names it a to j. notein fires channel \, then velocity \, then pitch \, so pack holds the bank and the velocity cold and the pitch sends all three., f 66;
#X text 1220 3640 param only: the row is u_map's (item 317). A playing 404 pattern transmits exactly like a hand (items 204 and 205) \, so its pads draw too \, and nothing can filter them out., f 66;
#X text 20 3880 Every event goes to param \, the release included: whether a release is worth a row is u_map's call., f 66;
#X text 1220 3880 The CTRL knobs \, named by raw CC number (sp-cc-16 \, sp-cc-17) like m_launchpad's ring., f 66;
#X text 2420 3880 The rate limit drops and never queues: there is no queue between Pd and the 404 \, and overshooting costs seconds of lag (item 209). A dropped trigger is gone \, and nothing is held back for later., f 66;
#X text 20 4120 A token bucket \, in the Lua: sixteen triggers at once \, so a step with every drum track on passes whole \, refilled at one per 5 ms \, 200 a second \, about half the 404's ceiling (item 208). timer measures the gap since the last trigger in Pd's own time \, and list append hands it over with the pad \, so nothing runs while nothing plays. A dropped trigger answers nothing \, so it leaves no orphan note-off., f 66;
#X text 1220 4120 The note-off carries its own channel through pipe: with makenote \, two banks overlapping would send the off to the wrong bank (ref/device/sp404.md). pipe's outlets fire right to left \, so noteout gets the channel before the note., f 66;
#X text 2420 4120 Panic covers all ten channels: the device's owner owns its panic., f 66;
#X text 20 4360 Prints the channel block it got: nothing the 404 sends says which block it landed on. C-9, f 66;
#X text 1220 4360 The reject is a real error \, as in m_volca. C-8, f 66;
#X obj 20 4620 c_devid 65;
#X obj 320 4620 r \$0-on;
#X obj 320 4680 select 1;
#X obj 620 4620 r \$0-cc-on;
#X obj 620 4680 select 1;
#X obj 20 4800 c_presence m_404 3 120;
#X msg 20 4880 240 \, 126 \, 127 \, 6 \, 1 \, 247;
#X obj 20 5100 midiout;
#X obj 320 4800 loadbang;
#X obj 320 4850 f \$1;
#X obj 320 4900 - 1;
#X obj 320 4950 div 16;
#X obj 320 5000 + 1;
#X text 900 4620 c_devid 65 is Roland's manufacturer byte \, 0x41 (item 249). The 120 ms stagger keeps three inquiry replies from interleaving on the one sysexin (ref/module/presence.md)., f 62;
#X text 900 4920 The port is derived from the channel block \, (block-1)/16+1 \, as in m_nano: midiout takes the port as a plain number \, where noteout's channel encodes it., f 62;
#X text 1900 4620 Two channel gates \, so two liveness taps: the notes and the CTRL knobs. A playing pattern counts \, rightly: a device that transmits is plugged in., f 62;
#X text 1900 4980 c_presence's second outlet stays unconnected: everything here is recomputed per event. The scheduled note-offs are left alone on a loss: the device may be back within 200 ms \, and if not they cost nothing., f 62;
#X obj 220 1020 pack f f f;
#X obj 20 2160 list append;
#X obj 600 2250 m_404-lua \$1;
#X obj 760 2400 s param;
#X obj 900 2400 s err;
#X msg 1040 2400 0;
#X obj 1100 2160 loadbang;
#X obj 1100 2210 t b b;
#X msg 1250 2290 init;
#X obj 1100 2500 spigot 1;
#X msg 1100 2550 fail m_404 no-lua;
#X obj 1100 2600 s err;
#X obj 2900 2200 declare -lib pdlua;
#X text 1220 2700 The decode is Lua: m_404-lua names a note on the ten channels sp-<bank><pad> \, and turns a pad to play into a note on its bank's channel and the note-off the pipe holds \, behind the budget. A note outside the pad map names nothing. The rules are m_404.lua \, tested without Pd by test/gate/lua/m_404_test.lua (ref/device/sp404.md)., f 60;
#X text 1220 2960 At load the Lua answers init with a bang on its last outlet \, which shuts the spigot. No bang means it never loaded -- pdlua missing \, or an error in the Lua -- and fail m_404 no-lua says so on the screen: no pad plays and none is named \, while the CTRL knobs \, panic and presence still work. A Lua error is fail m_404 lua-<rule> (C-12)., f 60;
